  - "Goblins love cybernetics and bionics."
extraction_notes: |
  - Rifts Conversion Book One printed 98-99 (file p099-p100). The Rifts conversion of the Palladium Fantasy Goblin, which is the `goblin` row. A separate class because a variant cannot cross systems.
  - S.D.C. is 10 here - "10, plus those gained from O.C.C. and physical skills" - where the Palladium Fantasy row carries 5. Stored as a POOL BONUS. The Spd line prints "3D6 (1D6 digging)"; the running figure is stored.
  - THE COBBLER IS PROSE, NOT A VARIANT. The Palladium row''s note walks through why: a variant''s `bonuses` REPLACE the class''s rather than merging, so stating the Cobbler''s saves would drop the Goblin''s own; and five of its parts - metamorphosis, six spells, the percentile roll, the psionics bar and the +10% skill bonuses - are not variant-overridable at all. A variant carrying only the P.P.E. would look complete and hold nothing the book calls significant. So the Cobbler is one natural_abilities entry, and a player who rolls one applies it by hand.
  - The Cobbler roll disagrees with itself on printed 98-99: the text calls a Cobbler "a one in 20 genetic mutant" and the procedure says 1-15 on percentile (15%). The procedure is recorded as the rule, and both are in the entry.
  - NOT MODELLED: +2% to Rogue/Thief skills, a per-skill modifier on skills the OCCUPATION grants.
  - occ_restrictions is an `except`, because "most any Man at Arms or Adventurer, except..." is an open list with named holes. It bars the magic, psychic and clergy groups, and names the military, pilot, lawman and highly skilled O.C.C.s the catalog holds today. "Highly skilled" is the book''s phrase and not a list; Operator, Cyber-Doc, Body Fixer, the Rogue Scientist and Scholar and the three scientist O.C.C.s are the reading. An O.C.C. of any of those kinds imported after this is allowed until it is added.
  - Psionics: "Standard, basically same as humans", so no psionics block.
  - Size three feet plus 2D6 inches; weight 60 to 100 pounds; life span 80 years. In the Lore.
  - The section-wide rule on printed 74 - a new arrival from the Palladium World picks up the regional language and two Modern W.P.s within weeks, then three Rifts skills from Communications, Pilot (basic vehicles), Technical and W.P. Modern after 2D4+4 months or one level, and one more language or skill every two levels - applies to a character who came from Palladium rather than one raised on Rifts Earth. It is not stored; the survey carries it.
